        "rationale": "The marked tests cover each obligation in `requirements.index.navigation`.\n\n- **Two adjacent links per declaration badge.** `declaration_sections_contain_their_headers_and_markdown_bodies` in `src/lib.rs` checks the header of both a `req` and an `example` declaration. The kind link has `href=\"#habeas-{kind}-rules.{name}\"` and the name link has `href=\"requirements-index/rules.{name}.html\"`. It also checks that both links sit in the summary header, not the body. `mdbook_preprocessor_renders_definitions_between_stdin_and_stdout` in `tests/repository.rs` checks the real binary's output. Each `habeas-definition-badge` row has exactly one `habeas-badge-kind` link, one `habeas-badge-name` link and two `</a>` tags. `declaration_badges_and_margin_controls_share_kind_colors` covers the `req` and `example` kinds.\n- **One non-wrapping row.** `declaration_badge_stylesheet_keeps_split_links_in_one_row` asserts `inline-flex`, `flex-wrap: nowrap`, `white-space: nowrap` and `flex-shrink: 0` on the wrapper and links.\n- **No arrow link and no plaintext evidence link.** `habeas-detail-icon` and `<svg` are asserted absent from the headers. \"See evidence\" is asserted absent in `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` and `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages`.\n- **Detail pages link to the anchored badge and to the index.** `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` in `src/index.rs` asserts `[Requirements index](../requirements-index.html) · [View definition](../../requirements/core.html#habeas-req-...)`. `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages` checks every detail page's index link and nested-chapter definition links. `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` covers an example declaration. `detail_pages_link_to_readme_chapters_at_their_index_output` covers a README chapter.\n- **Reference badges link to the declaration.** `references_in_nested_chapters_link_to_the_requirement_definition` asserts the `impl`, `cite` and `test` badges from `guides/deep.md` link to `../requirements.html#habeas-req-requirements.ready`.\n- **Links resolve when a name contains `.md`.** `links_preserve_requirement_names_containing_md` asserts the `chapter_href` outputs for both directions, giving `%2Emd` in the detail page link and in the anchor. `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages` and `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` assert the rendered `rules.cli%2Emdbook` badge and detail links. `reference_badge` builds its link through the same `chapter_href`, so the `.md` handling also applies to reference badges. There is no direct test of a reference badge to a `.md`-named requirement, but the shared helper is tested.\n\nAdditional tests, such as `definition_evidence_link_targets_are_escaped` and the README `chapter_href` test, add coverage. I found no unmet obligation and no ambiguity."
